A||||5||2birds||Tennessee emissions and registration questions, legal stuff...||||1||
Z||000000||2birds||12-09-2001||07:10 PM||||As some of you know, I'm getting transferred to Millington, TN next month.  I'm bringing the Fiero and my two Fords, and I have some questions about emisssions controls in the Memphis region.  I haven't had to deal with inspections, emissions or otherwise, in 8 years.  What does TN require?<P>I also would prefer to change my Fords to TN registration if possible.  The Fiero is registered in PA (my legal residence), but PA is a PITA to get anything changed unless you bring the car to the state, since they need VIN tracings and notary stuff.  How is TN for tags, price-wise?  Any military exemptions frothe personal property taxes (like GA and VA do)?<P>How about tint laws?  My T-bird has Florida legal tint (29/32).  Kinda like it now that I'm used to it.<P>And how about driver's license changeover?  Any strange things there?||||reg||1
Z||000001||WampusCat||12-09-2001||07:43 PM||||If you have an address in the City of Memphis, you have to get an emissions inspection.  Out of the city limits you don't really need anything, just show up at the county clerk's office with your title and/or registration and some $$.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2birds||12-09-2001||09:36 PM||||After seeing the crime level map that My7Fieros sent me, I don't think I'll be living in Memphis the city.  Probably couldn't afford it anyway.  Never been there yet, but everybody I've talked to about the place tells me to look north of Millington.  <P>Didn't know if TN has a state-wide emissions/safety inspection or not.  Mine would all pass emissions visually, but I've never sniffer-checked any of them.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||12-09-2001||10:37 PM||||Just like Wampus Cat said....if you live within the city limits of Memphis, then you have to go through inspection. If you dont (whether its the county or city of Millington or whatever), then you dont have to.<BR>Tags cost around $125 bucks in the city and around 90 or so for the county. Just bring your title to any of the county clerks offices, theres a million of them around town.<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||2birds||12-09-2001||10:47 PM||||cool.<P>Any tint law problems?||||reg||1
Z||000005||8Ball||12-09-2001||11:47 PM||||Don't know about in memphis, but on the other side of the state tint has to be really light. Not sure on numbers but might as well not have any  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
